%S A398796 2,8,116,3896,275878,39218664,11049639120,6173853012432,
%T A398796 6863700652866486,15220877212048865664,67421759349178816718628,
%U A398796 596944108822151544144357248,10567650485214119880826816025348,374109124164086784760948403730846128
%N A398796 Number of reducible flow graphs on n unlabeled nodes with self-loops allowed, counted up to isomorphism fixing the entry.
%C A398796 Reducible control-flow graphs with self-loops (a basic block may jump to itself) up to entry-preserving isomorphism.
%C A398796 Computed exactly by the equivariant Burnside recurrence (see _reducible_unlabeled in the linked program of A397968); a permutation with c cycles contributes an extra invariant self-loop factor 2^(c+1).
%D A398796 F. Harary and E. M. Palmer, Graphical Enumeration, Academic Press, NY, 1973.
%D A398796 M. S. Hecht and J. D. Ullman, Flow graph reducibility, SIAM J. Comput. 1 (1972), 188-202.
%D A398796 M. S. Hecht and J. D. Ullman, Characterizations of reducible flow graphs, J. ACM 21 (1974), 367-375.
%D A398796 R. W. Robinson, Counting digraphs with restrictions on the strong components, in T.-H. Ku (ed.), Combinatorics and Graph Theory '95, World Scientific, Singapore, 1995, pp. 343-354.
%D A398796 R. E. Tarjan, Testing flow graph reducibility, J. Comput. System Sci. 9 (1974), 355-365.
%F A398796 The same Burnside sum and equivariant SCC-region recurrence as the loopless entry-pointed version, with an additional factor 2^(c(mu)+1) for the invariant self-loops, where c(mu) is the number of cycles of the entry-fixing permutation.
%o A398796 (Python) unlabeled_reducible_sequence("unlabeled_reducible_cfgs_loops", 16) # See Python link in A397968 for program code.
%Y A398796 Cf. A397968 (loopless version), A351052.
%K A398796 nonn,new
%O A398796 1,1
%A A398796 _Gregory Morse_, Sep 07 2026
